🤖 AI Blind Assistant Robot (School Level – Using Waste + Simple Electronics)

No heavy coding, no complex AI words — but it will talk, warn, and help a blind person.

⸻

🔹 WHAT THIS ROBOT DOES (IN SIMPLE WORDS)

This robot helps a blind person by:

✅ Detecting obstacles in front
✅ Saying “STOP! ObSTACLE AHEAD”
✅ Giving sound warning (buzzer + voice)
✅ Showing that it is an AI assistant (for judges 😄)
✅ Made mostly from cardboard & waste materials

⸻

🔹 BASIC IDEA (HOW IT WORKS)
	1.	A distance sensor checks if something is in front
	2.	If an obstacle is close:
	•	Buzzer beeps 🔔
	•	Speaker says: “Please stop, obstacle ahead”
	3.	Robot does not move forward (for model)
	4.	Blind person gets warning in sound

👉 This is called Artificial Intelligence because:
	•	The robot senses
	•	Decides
	•	Acts automatically

⸻

🔹 MATERIALS REQUIRED (VERY IMPORTANT)

♻️ WASTE / CRAFT MATERIALS
	•	Cardboard boxes (Amazon / shoe box)
	•	Cardboard tubes (tissue roll)
	•	Old bottle caps (for eyes / wheels)
	•	Chart paper (labels)
	•	Rope or thread
	•	Glue / Fevicol
	•	Tape
	•	Marker pen
	•	Scissors / cutter (adult help)
